### 3. QUANTIFIED DECISION MATRIX (WEIGHTED SCORING)
Evaluate competing options using a 1–5 scale across 5 weighted dimensions:
- Impact (1 = Low, 5 = Transformative)
- Cost (1 = High Cost, 5 = Low Cost / High Efficiency)
- Risk (1 = Critical Risk, 5 = Low Risk / Safe)
- Time-to-Market (1 = Slow, 5 = Rapid)
- Complexity (1 = High Complexity, 5 = Low Complexity)

Formula:
Net Score = (Impact × W_1) + (Cost × W_2) + (Risk × W_3) + (Time × W_4) + (Complexity × W_5)

Prioritize and recommend options strictly based on the highest Net Score.

